<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ostend Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1722">1722</a>–<a href="/years/1731">1731</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ostend Company was a trading company chartered by Emperor Charles VI in 1722 to trade from the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">East Indies</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Operating from Ostend, it made large profits in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> trade and set up posts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Under pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, Charles VI suspended its charter in 1727 and abolished it by the Second Treaty of Vienna in 1731.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ostend-company.jpg" alt="Ostend Company" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maryland u/FoulCoke · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ostend_company_flag.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
